course: dictionary
lesson: 10590
title: Working out underpass
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from its parts and the words around it. Under and pass together give a clue: an underpass is a way you pass under something. «Sam suggested a joint art project: a long mural on the underpass wall.» A mural is a painting on a wall, so an underpass has walls you can paint, and you walk through it.
explain: «Railways are only crossed by bridges, underpasses or proper level crossings.» This list names three ways to cross a railway. A bridge goes over the railway, and a level crossing is where the road and railway meet at the same height. So an underpass must be the third way: a route that goes under the railway.
explain: Check your idea by swapping it into the sentence. Try «go through the path under the road» in place of «go through the underpass». It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: An underpass is a road or path that goes under another road or a railway.
fact: People walk or cycle through an underpass so they can cross safely without meeting traffic.
fact: Phrases you may see are «go through the underpass» and «pedestrian underpass».
fact: A bridge goes over a road or railway, but an underpass goes under it.
fact: Safety rule: if an underpass is dark or empty, go with an adult.
exercise: What is an underpass? | A painting on a wall | *A road or path that goes under another road or a railway | A tall tower on a hill | A bridge that goes over a river
exercise: «Railways are only crossed by bridges, underpasses or proper level crossings.» Which way crosses a railway by going under it? | A bridge over the railway | *An underpass | A mural on a wall | A level crossing
exercise: Why should you go with an adult if the underpass is dark or empty? | *Because it may be less safe when it is dark or empty | Because the mural is painted there | Because underpasses are only for grown-ups | Because dark places are fun to explore
test: In «a long mural on the underpass wall», where is the mural? | In a field | *On the wall of an underpass | Inside a school bus | On the top of a hill
test: What is the safest way for a walker to cross a busy road? | Run across between the cars | *Use an underpass or a footbridge | Wait in the middle of the road | Cross at a bend where drivers cannot see
exam: Which way crosses a railway by going under it? | A bridge over the railway | A mural on a wall | *An underpass | A level crossing
